---
code: K0035
title: Test Without Name
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, test, unit-testing]
description: "'test' declaration is missing a plain string name"
---

A `test` declaration must be immediately followed by a plain, double-quoted string literal naming the test (`test "name" { ... }`). Unquoted identifiers, missing names, or strings containing `{...}` interpolations are not allowed.

## Example

This error occurs when `test` is followed directly by `{`, an identifier, or an interpolated string:

```kura
test {
  assert(1 + 1 == 2)
}

let label = "addition"
test "{label}" {
  assert(1 + 1 == 2)
}
```

## Solution

Provide a plain string literal name between `test` and the `{ ... }` test body:

```kura
test "addition" {
  assert(1 + 1 == 2)
}
```
